  "summary": {
   "status": "complete",
   "text": "In a March 2026 interview, Chris Klomp said fee schedules tend to be inflationary and not tied to outcomes, and that he was averse to creating an AI-specific fee schedule. In September 2026 remarks, he said prior authorization has largely not been used appropriately and can undermine trust between providers and patients, while calling it an appropriate utilization management tool when used precisely and appropriately. He also said he understood that inappropriate care denials carry significant financial penalties and that CMMI monitors performance and can terminate.",
   "sids": [
    "s1",
    "s3",
    "s4"
   ],
   "sentences": [
